.TH "grommunio\-admin\-chat" "1" "" "" ""
.SH Name
grommunio\-admin chat \[em] Chat management
.SH Synopsis
.PP
\f[B]grommunio\-admin chat\f[R] \f[B]remove\-all\f[R]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]grommunio\-admin chat\f[R] \f[B]sso\f[R] (\f[I]enable\f[R] |
\f[I]disable\f[R]) [\f[I]\-d DOMAIN\f[R]] \&...
.SH Description
Commands for the grommunio\-chat integration.
.SH Commands
.TP
\f[CR]remove\-all\f[R]
Set the chat IDs of all domains and users to NULL.
.TP
\f[CR]sso\f[R]
Move the chat accounts of grommunio users to single sign\-on through the
grommunio Keycloak realm (\f[I]enable\f[R]) or back to the local login
(\f[I]disable\f[R]), and set the defaults for new accounts accordingly.
Which OAuth service is used depends on what the chat server offers.
grommunio\-auth runs this when it configures grommunio\-chat.
.SH Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-d DOMAIN\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-domain DOMAIN\f[R]
Only affect users of DOMAIN and set its domain defaults.
Can be given multiple times.
Without this option the system defaults are set and per\-domain
overrides are removed.
